{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookFormulaBeta","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookFormulaBeta","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Intervals","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProd_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProd_pos","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBeta.lean#L195-L205","doc":"**`betaGapProd` is positive (sorry-free).** For a tail `t` with every part `≤ a`, each beta-gap\nfactor `a + 1 − c` is `≥ 1`, so the product is `> 0`.  (This is the strict decrease of the beta\nnumbers; it makes the Vandermonde denominator invertible in the dimension identity.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProd_mul_betaGapProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProd_mul_betaGapProd","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBeta.lean#L173-L193","doc":"**Per-row Frame–Robinson–Thrall hook product, divisor-free closed form (sorry-free).** For a\nweakly-decreasing tail `t` with every part `≤ a`,\n\n    rowHookProd a t · betaGapProd a t = (a + |t|)!.\n\nThis is `∏_{c ∈ row i} h(i,c) = β_i! / ∏_{j>i}(β_i − β_j)` (the per-row hook product of the\nbeta-number HLF) cleared of its denominator.  Proved by induction on the tail via the recursion\n`rowHookProd_cons_mul`; no division, no archimedean input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProd_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProd_cons","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBeta.lean#L170-L171","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProd_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProd_nil","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBeta.lean#L168-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProd","kind":"def","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBeta.lean#L161-L166","doc":"The beta-gap product `D a t = ∏_{j>i}(β_i − β_j)` in divisor-free, recursion-matched form:\n`D a [] = 1`, `D a (c :: r) = (a + 1 − c) · D (a+1) r`.  Each factor is the consecutive beta-gap as\nthe row index advances. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProd_cons_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProd_cons_mul","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBeta.lean#L92-L157","doc":"**Inductive step (sorry-free).** `rowHookProd a (c :: r) · (a + 1 − c) = rowHookProd (a+1) r`,\nfor `c ≤ a` and a weakly-decreasing tail `r` with every part `≤ c`.  The factor `(a + 1 − c)` is the\nbeta-gap `β_i − β_{i+1}`; the proof reindexes the row-`i` product against `g j = (a+1−j) + cnt r j`\n(the `a+1` row product), supplying the missing middle factor `g c = a + 1 − c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProd_eq_finset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProd_eq_finset","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBeta.lean#L86-L90","doc":"`rowHookProd` as a `Finset.range` product (the flexible form for reindexing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.list_range_map_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.list_range_map_prod","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBeta.lean#L77-L84","doc":"Bridge a `List.range`-mapped product to the corresponding `Finset.range` product (fixed `f`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProd_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProd_nil","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBeta.lean#L63-L75","doc":"**Base case (sorry-free).** With an empty tail the leg vanishes and the hook product is the\ndescending product `∏_{j<a}(a − j) = a!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowHookProd","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBeta.lean#L59-L61","doc":"**The per-row hook product** `∏_{j<a} ((a − j) + cnt t j)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.cnt_eq_zero_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.cnt_eq_zero_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBeta.lean#L50-L57","doc":"If every part of `t` is `≤ j`, the column-`j` leg is empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.cnt_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.cnt_cons","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBeta.lean#L43-L48","doc":"`cnt` recursion on a cons: prepending `c` adds one iff `j < c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.cnt_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.cnt_nil","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBeta.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.cnt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.cnt","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBeta.lean#L38-L39","doc":"`cnt t j = #{p ∈ t : p > j}` — the column-`j` leg contribution of the tail `t`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}